c A hand-written UNSAT instance on which a substitution rewrites one clause into another's
c span, so the rewritten clause is evicted and its line deleted. Solve with --bve=false
c --otf-subsume=false.
c The first two clauses refute x3 = 1 by propagation, so the first conflict learns the unit
c x3 = 0. Its substitution rewrites the fourth clause, x1 + x3 = 1 or x2 = 1, into the third,
c x1 = 1 or x2 = 1, which is kept while the fourth is evicted.
c Once x3 = 0, the last sixteen clauses rule out x1 = 1 and x2 = 1 through every sign pattern
c over x5, x6, x7, so only search refutes the rest, and it cites the third clause.
c BVE would derive x3 = 0 before any search by eliminating x4, and on-the-fly subsumption
c would add evictions of its own to the count.
p xnf 7 20
-3 4 0
-3 -4 0
1 2 0
1+3 2 0
3 -1 5 6 7 0
3 -1 5 6 -7 0
3 -1 5 -6 7 0
3 -1 5 -6 -7 0
3 -1 -5 6 7 0
3 -1 -5 6 -7 0
3 -1 -5 -6 7 0
3 -1 -5 -6 -7 0
3 -2 5 6 7 0
3 -2 5 6 -7 0
3 -2 5 -6 7 0
3 -2 5 -6 -7 0
3 -2 -5 6 7 0
3 -2 -5 6 -7 0
3 -2 -5 -6 7 0
3 -2 -5 -6 -7 0
